<title>AUSTRALIA: SWIMMING-MITCHELL SETS WORLD BREASTSTROKE RECORD.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-MITCHELL SETS WORLD BREASTSTROKE RECORD.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-12-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's Ryan Mitchell set a short-course world record for the men's 200 metres breaststroke at the national short-course swimming championships on Saturday.</p>
<p>Mitchell clocked two minutes 7.66 seconds to beat the mark of 2:07.80 set in the same pool in 1993 by his training partner Phil Rogers.</p>
